                <pb facs="0657" n="649" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg649"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.51/39: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-09-23T13:00:00+02:00">September 23, 1941—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 24—8:23 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1454. Department’s 453, September 10, 9 a.m. [<hi rendition="#italic">p.m.</hi>].
                    In view of the directives given in Department’s telegram under reference I have
                    addressed a reply to the Minister of Foreign Affairs of Saudi Arabia drafted as
                    closely along the lines of the Department’s 399, August 22, 8 p.m., as
                    safeguarding of the codes permitted.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
